#!/usr/bin/env xetal
## A subway map written by its station names: g_raph< defines a variable
## per station and the map as a matrix when the program is compiled, so
## the program speaks of stations, not numbers. Run with "just demo Graphs stations".

"g:" u_se< "Graphs"
"town" g:g_raph< "airport-bridge-center-docks-exchange, fair-center-garden, docks-harbor"
town
center                                    # its number
town g:l_evels center                     # stops from the center to each station
harbor s_elect town g:l_evels airport    # stops from the airport to the harbor
